  "things_i_could_not_establish_as_consumer_visible_and_therefore_left_out": [
    "**`SearchFilter.attributes: Vec<(String, String)>` (the EAV / filterable pre-KNN axis).** It is a new PUBLIC Rust struct field, but I could not find any Python or TypeScript route to it: the SDK `Filter` grammar is closed at exactly five term variants (source_type, kind, created_after, status, json) in both bindings, and the Python `SearchFilter` dataclass is byte-identical to v0.8.9. So the `filterable` role is declarable via configure_projections but I could not establish that a consumer can QUERY on an attribute from Python or TypeScript. I wrote no line claiming they can. WORTH A TARGETED CHECK before publish — if there IS a route, it deserves an Added bullet.",
    "**Whether `rankable` has any consumer-observable effect at 0.8.20.** It is a valid ProjectionRole and is named in the registry entry as one of the three members, but I did not find a shipped ranking behaviour a consumer can turn on (the F9 reweight it would feed is off with no production toggle). I deliberately did not write a bullet claiming rankable does something.",
