    "**Several new `*_for_test` public Rust fns** (arm_reader_search_hook_for_test, clock_reads_for_test, query_i64_col_for_test, secure_delete_enabled_for_test, …). Public by Rust visibility but plainly test seams; not announced.",
    "**`ExciseRecordReport`, `ProjectionFts`, `ProjectionVector`, `RowKind`, `Bm25fFieldWeights`, `Bm25fQueryPlan`, `InitialState`, `IdSpaceKind`, `DenseReadiness`, `LifecycleState`** — all net-new public Rust types. The ones with a consumer story are named inside their owning feature entry; the rest (Bm25f*, RowKind) are not announced because I could not state what a consumer does with them.",
    "**A precise 'first release with X' attribution for a few items.** `search_text_only` reached TypeScript at 0.8.18 (f2f843ed) but the Python stub only at 0.8.20 (0457908c, the ReadView slice). Because every intermediate version was label-only, this distinction is invisible to a consumer stepping 0.8.9 -> 0.8.20, so I attributed the feature to 0.8.18 (where the behaviour landed) rather than write a two-date caveat. Flagging it as a simplification, not a verified single-date fact."
